{"id": "EUVD-2026-108301", "enisaUuid": "c2ba6c10-61cf-30a3-9cc7-1e666172c4a2", "description": "Incus before 6.0.7, 6.1.0 before 7.0.2, and 7.1.0 before 7.5.0 contains an arbitrary file write vulnerability in sftpRecursivePullFile that allows a malicious incus-agent to escape the target directory during incus file pull -r. Attackers with root in a virtual machine can return duplicate entries reported first as symlinks then as files or directories, writing attacker-controlled files such as /etc/shadow on the operator's host.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T19:13:47", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T19:13:47", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:P/VC:N/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:H/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/lxc/incus/security/advisories/GHSA-wfvq-qh87-gm4j", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/incus-before-6.0.7-6.1.0-before-7.0.2-and-7.1.0-before-7.5.0-arbitrary-file-write-via-recursive-file-pull"], "aliases": ["GHSA-38pq-92hw-9rp6", "CVE-2026-115378"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "852da835-914c-36da-9a7b-0ef6aa28dd17", "product": {"name": "incus", "vendor": {"name": "lxc"}}, "product_version": "6.1.0 <7.0.2"}, {"id": "9d694613-2c3f-3877-bf81-540d04d126f1", "product": {"name": "incus", "vendor": {"name": "lxc"}}, "product_version": "7.1.0 <7.5.0"}, {"id": "fa213e00-4dcd-381b-af6d-38d35442070a", "product": {"name": "incus", "vendor": {"name": "lxc"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.0.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "bbd85c87-8181-3649-a4a0-7ec5cc0b07e4", "vendor": {"name": "lxc"}}], "isExploited": false}